meta {
  name: Update Entries Scopes
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/parlance.v1.EntryService/UpdateEntriesScopes
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept-Language: en
}

body:json {
  {
    "entryIds": ["{{entryId}}"],
    "addScopeIds": ["{{scopeId}}"],
    "removeScopeIds": []
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Entries Scopes

  Adds and removes scopes on several entries at once.

  ## Authentication
  Requires the `update_entry` permission. User ID is tracked as updater on every entry.

  ## Request
  - `entryIds` (required): UUIDs of the entries to update, at most 1000
  - `addScopeIds` (optional): scopes to add; scopes an entry already has are kept
  - `removeScopeIds` (optional): scopes to remove; ignored where an entry doesn't have them

  ## Behavior
  - Scopes not listed are left unchanged
  - All entries are updated in one transaction

  ## Errors
  - `INVALID_ARGUMENT`: no entries, no scopes, too many entries, a scope in both lists, or an unknown scope to add
  - `NOT_FOUND`: one or more entries do not exist
  - `INTERNAL`: failed to update entry scopes
}
